	Synchronization (Waits in selenium)
	Synchronization is adjusting execution speed of tool with speed of application. 
	


	Methods in selenium to handle synchronization
	1. Thread.sleep();
		a. it pauses the entire execution for given time period.
		b. it is applicable for single statement only.
		c. Mandatory delay (it take mandatory time, 1,2,3)
		
	2. Implicit wait (global wait)
		a. it doesn't takes a mandatory delay(if element loads within 2 seconds then it will not wait for given time period)
		b. default polling interval is 500 milisecond (.5 second) 
		c. Existence of element --> present of element --> display of element
		d. Only checks the existence of an element. 
		e. Stops early as soon as gets the element
		f. for given time period, implicit wait can ignore only NOSuchElementException (10 second)
		g. Applies for each line of code which starts from driver.findelement or driver.findelements
	 
	
	3. Explicit wait
		a. it doesn't takes a mandatory delay(if element loads within 2 seconds then it will not wait for given time period)
		b. default polling interval is 500 milisecond (.5 second) 
		c. checks the existence of element along with other states of elements also(presence, enabling, appears, disappear etc.)
		
		Syntax :
		WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(5)); // 15 seconds
		wait.until(ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated(By.cssSelector("div[aria-label^='Lal Ghati']")))
				.click();
				
				
		Notes: lets say am using 
		impiclitwait - 10
		
	4. FluentWait -
		a. it doesn't takes a mandatory delay(if element loads within 2 seconds then it will not wait for given time period)
		b. customize polling wait is allow.
		c. check all type of state of an element
		d. customize to all any exceptions
		
		Syntax
		FluentWait<WebDriver> fWait = new FluentWait<WebDriver>(driver);
		fWait.withTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(10)).ignoring(NoSuchElementException.class)
		.ignoring(StaleElementReferenceException.class)
		.pollingEvery(Duration.ofSeconds(2))
		.until(ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated(By.cssSelector("div[aria-label^='Lal Ghati']")))
		.click();
		
